Claude Code Hooks
Hooks are shell commands (or HTTP/MCP/prompt/agent calls) that execute at fixed lifecycle points in Claude Code’s workflow. They provide deterministic control over behaviour that shouldn’t depend on the LLM’s choices — validation, formatting, blocking, notifications.
See also: Claude Code Settings (where hooks are configured), Claude Code Orchestration

Hook Types
Five types are available, configured with a &quot;type&quot; field:
command — Run a shell script
{
  &quot;type&quot;: &quot;command&quot;,
  &quot;command&quot;: &quot;./.claude/hooks/validate.sh&quot;,
  &quot;args&quot;: [&quot;--strict&quot;],
  &quot;async&quot;: false,
  &quot;asyncRewake&quot;: false,
  &quot;shell&quot;: &quot;bash&quot;
}
Receives the tool invocation as JSON on stdin. Communicates back via exit code + stdout/stderr.
http — POST to a URL
{
  &quot;type&quot;: &quot;http&quot;,
  &quot;url&quot;: &quot;example.com/hook&quot;,
  &quot;headers&quot;: { &quot;Authorization&quot;: &quot;Bearer $MY_TOKEN&quot; },
  &quot;allowedEnvVars&quot;: [&quot;MY_TOKEN&quot;]
}
mcp_tool — Call an MCP server tool
{
  &quot;type&quot;: &quot;mcp_tool&quot;,
  &quot;server&quot;: &quot;server_name&quot;,
  &quot;tool&quot;: &quot;tool_name&quot;,
  &quot;input&quot;: { &quot;path&quot;: &quot;${tool_input.file_path}&quot; }
}
prompt — Single-turn yes/no Claude evaluation
{
  &quot;type&quot;: &quot;prompt&quot;,
  &quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Does this bash command look destructive? $ARGUMENTS&quot;,
  &quot;model&quot;: &quot;fast_model&quot;
}
agent — Spawn a subagent for complex evaluation
{
  &quot;type&quot;: &quot;agent&quot;,
  &quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Audit this file change for security issues: $ARGUMENTS&quot;,
  &quot;model&quot;: &quot;claude-sonnet-4-6&quot;
}

