Tool names: Bash, Edit, Write, Read, Glob, Grep, Agent, WebFetch, WebSearch, AskUserQuestion, plus MCP tools.

Exit Codes (command hooks)





















CodeMeaning0Success — parse JSON from stdout2Blocking error — use stderr as error message, stop the tool callOtherNon-blocking error — show stderr only

JSON Output Format
A hook can return JSON to influence Claude’s behaviour:
{
  &quot;continue&quot;: true,
  &quot;stopReason&quot;: &quot;message if continue=false&quot;,
  &quot;suppressOutput&quot;: false,
  &quot;systemMessage&quot;: &quot;warning shown to user&quot;,
  &quot;decision&quot;: &quot;block&quot;,
  &quot;reason&quot;: &quot;why it was blocked&quot;,
  &quot;hookSpecificOutput&quot;: {
    &quot;hookEventName&quot;: &quot;PreToolUse&quot;,
    &quot;additionalContext&quot;: &quot;extra context for Claude&quot;,
    &quot;permissionDecision&quot;: &quot;allow|deny|ask|defer&quot;
  }
}

Key Flags

































FlagEffect&quot;async&quot;: trueRun in background without blocking Claude&quot;asyncRewake&quot;: trueWake Claude on exit code 2 from async hook&quot;once&quot;: trueRun only once per session&quot;if&quot;: &quot;Bash(rm *)&quot;Conditional — only run if expression matches&quot;timeout&quot;: NMax seconds before hook times out&quot;statusMessage&quot;: &quot;…&quot;Status bar text while hook runs
Identical handlers are deduplicated — the same command/URL runs only once even if multiple hooks would fire it.

Practical Examples
Block destructive rm -rf
{
  &quot;hooks&quot;: {
    &quot;PreToolUse&quot;: [{
      &quot;matcher&quot;: &quot;Bash&quot;,
      &quot;hooks&quot;: [{
        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;command&quot;,
        &quot;command&quot;: &quot;./.claude/hooks/block-rm.sh&quot;
      }]
    }]
  }
}
#!/bin/bash
tool_info=$(cat)
if echo &quot;$tool_info&quot; | grep -q &#039;rm -rf&#039;; then
  echo &quot;Destructive command blocked&quot; &gt;&amp;2
  exit 2
fi
exit 0
Auto-format after edits
{
  &quot;hooks&quot;: {
    &quot;PostToolUse&quot;: [{
      &quot;matcher&quot;: &quot;Edit&quot;,
      &quot;hooks&quot;: [{ &quot;type&quot;: &quot;command&quot;, &quot;command&quot;: &quot;prettier --write $file_path&quot; }]
    }]
  }
}
macOS notification on session start
{
  &quot;hooks&quot;: {
    &quot;SessionStart&quot;: [{
      &quot;matcher&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,
      &quot;hooks&quot;: [{
        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;command&quot;,
        &quot;command&quot;: &quot;osascript -e &#039;display notification \&quot;Claude Code started\&quot;&#039;&quot;
      }]
    }]
  }
}
Debug path-scoped rule loading
{
  &quot;hooks&quot;: {
    &quot;InstructionsLoaded&quot;: [{
      &quot;matcher&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,
      &quot;hooks&quot;: [{
        &quot;type&quot;: &quot;command&quot;,
        &quot;command&quot;: &quot;echo &#039;Loaded: $ARGUMENTS&#039; &gt;&gt; /tmp/claude-debug.log&quot;
      }]
    }]
  }
}

Temporarily Disable All Hooks
{ &quot;disableAllHooks&quot;: true }
Browse active hooks with /hooks.

