Hooks Configuration
Hooks live inside settings.json under &quot;hooks&quot;. See Claude Code Hooks for the full reference on types, lifecycle events, matchers, and output format.
Quick example — run linting after every file edit:
{
  &quot;hooks&quot;: {
    &quot;PostToolUse&quot;: [
      {
        &quot;matcher&quot;: &quot;Edit&quot;,
        &quot;hooks&quot;: [{ &quot;type&quot;: &quot;command&quot;, &quot;command&quot;: &quot;prettier --write $file_path&quot; }]
      }
    ]
  }
}

Sandbox (Bash Isolation)
Restrict which filesystem paths and network hosts Bash commands can access:
{
  &quot;sandbox&quot;: {
    &quot;enabled&quot;: true,
    &quot;filesystem&quot;: [&quot;~/**&quot;, &quot;/tmp/**&quot;],
    &quot;network&quot;: [&quot;api.example.com&quot;, &quot;*.github.com&quot;]
